Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: arm/palette_neon_intrinsics.c
Line: 112
Function: png_target_do_expand_palette_rgb8_neon
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: In the same loop, for row_width not a multiple of 8 and > 8, sp is moved before the start of the source row (e.g., sp = *ssp - 8 then accesses *(sp - 7)), resulting in reads from memory preceding the source buffer.

Source context:
```c
